    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 11,
        "x": 13,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Reading this dashboard\n\nEverything here is **scraped** \u2014 counts, depths, durations. Losses and accuracies are not here and never will be: they belong to a *step*, not to a moment, and a scraper on a timer would record them against the wrong axis (ADR 0009). They are on **AshML \u2014 Training curves**, read from `training_metrics` over the PostgreSQL datasource.\n\nScheduling latency has a floor built into it: the executor polls (`ASHML_EXECUTOR_INTERVAL_MS`, 2 s by default), so a job waits on average half an interval before anything looks at it. A p50 far *below* one second means submissions are phase-locked to the poll cycle, not that scheduling got fast \u2014 that exact artefact is written up in `docs/benchmarks.md`."
      },
      "transparent": false
    },
