    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Launch outcomes",
      "description": "`launched` created a Kubernetes Job. `requeued` means the job was claimed and put back \u2014 nothing fit, or quota refused it \u2014 which is normal and is how head-of-line blocking is avoided. `error` is the launch itself throwing, which leaves the job in SCHEDULING for the next pass to retry rather than failing the user's job for the platform's outage.",
